Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:44:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/17] qt: theme the QtWidgets dialogs with the Omarchy
 palette

OmarchyTheme::widgetPalette() maps the theme to QPalette roles (pure data, tested,
text raised to 4.5:1 against its surface). MainCtx applies it to the application
palette while the Omarchy scheme is active and restores the style's palette
otherwise; it is applied once at start-up because currentChanged is silent when the
saved index equals the default. The busy-progress stylesheet follows the palette
instead of hard-coded white and orange. Dialog layouts are untouched.
